)/S/GoTo>>endobj330 0 obj<</A 332 0 R/Next 333 0 R/Parent 327 0 R/Title(1. Roof mounted units exposed to winds may require wind baffles.)>>endobj331 0 obj<</A 334 0 R/Parent 327 0 R/Prev 335 0 R/Title(Fig. 1 … Connecting Tubing Installation)>>endobj334 0 obj<</D(G1450539)/S/GoTo>>endobj335 0 obj<</A 336 0 R/Next 331 0 R/Parent 327 0 R/Prev 337 0 R/Title(18. When setting up refrigerant piping, precautions shall be taken to avoid excessive vibration or pulsation)>>endobj336 0 obj<</D(G1544885)/S/GoTo>>endobj337 0 obj<</A 338 0 R/Next 335 0 R/Parent 327 0 R/Prev 339 0 R/Title(17. Piping material, routing, and installation shall include protection from physical damage in operation and service, and be in compliance with the national and local codes and standards of the installation site.)>>endobj338 0 obj<</D(G1544894)/S/GoTo>>endobj339 0 obj<</A 340 0 R/Next 337 0 R/Parent 327 0 R/Prev 341 0 R/Title(16. Flexible pipe elements shall be protected against mechanical damage, excessive stress by torsion, or other forces. They should be checked for mechanical damage annually.)>>endobj340 0 obj<</D(G1544893)/S/GoTo>>endobj341 0 obj<</A 342 0 R/Next 339 0 R/Parent 327 0 R/Prev 343 0 R/Title(15. Certified piping and components must be used in order to protect against corrosion.)>>endobj342 0 obj<</D(G1544892)/S/GoTo>>endobj343 0 obj<</A 344 0 R/Next 341 0 R/Parent 327 0 R/Prev 345 0 R/Title(14. Piping should be installed to reduce the likelihood of hydraulic shock damaging the system.)>>endobj344 0 obj<</D(G1544891)/S/GoTo>>endobj345 0 obj<</A 346 0 R/Next 343 0 R/Parent 327 0 R/Prev 347 0 R/Title(13. Piping and fittings shall be protected as far as possible against adverse environmental effects. For example, the accumulation of dirt and debris.)>>endobj346 0 obj<</D(G1544890)/S/GoTo>>endobj347 0 obj<</A 348 0 R/Next 345 0 R/Parent 327 0 R/Prev 349 0 R/Title(12. Provision shall be made for expansion and contraction of long runs of 